      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "pointSize": 5,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (increase(sbproxy_operator_fallback_probes_total[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "The Kubernetes operator asking each proxy pod whether it is serving a configuration its boot fallback restored. outcome=\"pinned\" means config delivery to that SBProxy is suspended and an operator has to clear the pin with DELETE /admin/config/fallback. Every other non-configured outcome is a fail-open the operator takes deliberately: \"unreachable\", \"refused\" and \"unreadable\" all mean it could not ask and reconciled anyway, so a series climbing there is a suspension that has silently stopped working. \"unowned\" means a pod carried the SBProxy's instance label but was not created by its workload; it was not probed and was not sent the admin credential, and a non-zero rate is worth looking at. \"budget_exhausted\" means the fleet is larger than one pass can probe."
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "title": "Operator Config Delivery",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
