          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (state) (increase(sbproxy_operator_config_delivery_total[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{state}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Whether configuration is still reaching each SBProxy's pods, and if not, why. sbproxy_operator_reconcile_total answers \"did the pass finish\", and every refusal here finishes cleanly, so it reads ok; this is the series that says the ConfigMap and workload were not applied. state=\"delivered\" is the healthy one. \"suspended_on_fallback\" means a pod is serving a config its boot fallback restored and an operator has to clear the pin. \"refused_auto_revert\" is permanent until somebody edits the config: the document arms proxy.config_history.soak.auto_revert, which loses a race with this operator. \"refused_acme\" and \"refused_invalid_config\" are the two pre-existing guards, now visible in metrics rather than only on the CR's lastError."
    }
